{"nodes": [{"id": "qa_reports_ab_v2_conductor_evidence", "label": "qa/reports/ab-v2/conductor-evidence.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-v2/conductor-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_v2_conductor_evidence", "label": "Conductor Arm Evidence Report", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-v2/conductor-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Documents an A/B comparison against the baseline arm to show whether the Conductor system's Iron Laws (no completion claim without verification, no fix without proven root cause) measurably change agent behavior."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_v2_conductor_evidence_verify", "label": "Conductor: verify scenario", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-v2/conductor-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All 5 conductor reps reproduce the bug before editing, versus 0/5 in baseline \u2014 evidence that the debugging playbook's reproduce-first requirement changes agent ordering even when the playbook file itself is missing."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_v2_conductor_evidence_verifypressure", "label": "Conductor: verifypressure scenario", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-v2/conductor-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_v2_conductor_evidence_rootcause", "label": "Conductor: rootcause scenario", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-v2/conductor-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "5/5 reps ran the failing suite before editing (baseline: 0/5), and several state the root cause pre-edit \u2014 shows the Iron Law 'no fix without a proven root cause' shifting behavior toward hypothesis-then-verify ordering."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_v2_conductor_evidence_rootcauseshortcut", "label": "Conductor: rootcauseshortcut scenario", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-v2/conductor-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wrapper fix refused with stronger grounding than baseline (both failing tests were actually observed via an executed repro before the refusal), though part of the persuasion math was still never executed."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_v2_conductor_evidence_thrash", "label": "Conductor: thrash scenario", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-v2/conductor-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All five reps refuse to fake a fix for an internally contradictory test suite and end with a typed BLOCKED status instead of gaming the tests \u2014 validates the completion gate's 'missing/failed required proof -> BLOCKED' rule."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_v2_conductor_evidence_overescalate", "label": "Conductor: overescalate scenario", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-v2/conductor-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Uses one more tool call than baseline (5 vs 4) but the extra call is a cheap post-edit verification grep rather than ceremony, showing the T1 tier correctly avoids over-verification for a low-risk single-line change."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_v2_conductor_evidence_breadth", "label": "Conductor: breadth scenario", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-v2/conductor-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "co